      "writtenOn": "2021-05-21T04:16:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I thought min_sdk_version 29 is all you needed. It means \"I want to run on a device with API version 29 or greater\".\n\nsdk_version 29 for a native binary means \"show my only symbols that existed in SDK 29\". But often we want to see newer APIs so we can conditionally use them with a runtime check.\n\nBut I have a question for Remi: why did we need to explicitly request sdk_version current? The DnsResolver does not require any of that.",
